An 8-week MBSR (Mindfulness-Based Stress Reduction) programme reduces salivary cortisol by a mean of 13% compared to control, according to a 2013 meta-analysis in Health Psychology.
MRI studies show that regular meditators have measurably thicker prefrontal cortices and smaller amygdalae — structural brain changes correlating with lower stress reactivity.
The telomere length of long-term meditators (a marker of biological ageing) is significantly greater than age-matched non-meditators, suggesting reduced cellular-level stress burden.
